- Gradient descent is most popular algo to update the weights of neural network.



- Decisions has to be taken to optimize one or more objectives
under some prescribed set of circumstances.

- Numerical optimisation: Decision making, Quantitative, objectives, variables,
constraint.

1) Quantify elements: objectives (goal), variables(decision we make, ex: to select or not), constraints, parameters(values fixed in problem)
2) Solution procedure: Solver, Algo, Metaheuristics
3) Evaluate results: tables, plots

- When using heuristics, we know the underlying problem and thus use some 
some features of the given problem. They are problem dependent.
Tailored solution that work for specific problem types.

- Problem in metaheuristics are problem independent. We know nothing about the underlying problem
we want to solve.They are designed to be general frameworks that can be applied to 
various types of problem. Thus they have broader applicability.

Pyomo:
-----
- open source python based algebraic modeling language.
- Creates the structure of optimisation models used by solvers
- Model is core element here. All elements are included in model 
as attributes
- Two alternatives: ConcreteModel(data comes in as elements are created), AbstractModel(Data comes in later)






